# Routing and Navigation Rules

## Expo Router File-Based Routing

- Routes defined by file structure in `app/` directory
- File names map to routes
- Folders create route segments
- `_layout.tsx` files define layout for route groups

## Route Groups

- Parentheses create route groups: `(auth)`, `(noAuth)`
- Groups organize routes without affecting URL
- Each group has `_layout.tsx` for layout configuration
- Groups can have nested groups

## Protected Routes

- Use `Redirect` component in layout files
- Check authentication state in layout
- Redirect to login if not authenticated
- Redirect to app if authenticated
- Example: `app/(auth)/_layout.tsx` checks session

## Navigation Patterns

- Use `router.replace()` for navigation that replaces history
- Use `router.push()` for navigation that adds to history
- Use `router.back()` for going back
- Navigation triggered from context providers or components

## Stack and Tabs Navigators

- Use `Stack` from `expo-router` for stack navigation
- Use `Tabs` from `expo-router` for tab navigation
- Configure screen options in layout files
- Headers configured per screen or globally

## Dynamic Routes

- Use brackets for dynamic segments: `[id]`
- Access params via `useLocalSearchParams()` or route options
- Example: `app/(auth)/devices/[id].tsx` for device details

## Route Configuration

- Screen options set in `_layout.tsx` files
- Use i18n for screen titles
- Custom headers with components
- Header backgrounds and styling via options

## Routing Rules

- Routes MUST follow file-based structure
- Protected routes MUST check auth in layout
- Navigation MUST use expo-router methods
- Screen titles MUST use i18n
- Route groups MUST have `_layout.tsx` files
